yuji.choreography:
Use case: stylized-concept. Create a production battle sprite atlas for a Jujutsu Kaisen HD-2D browser RPG.
Reference 1 is the USER-APPROVED B pixel style, not a subject reference. Reference 2 is official character identity. Follow reference 2 faithfully for hair, clothing, anatomy, accessories; render in reference 1's compact refined pixel style: crisp stepped pixel clusters, deliberate small pixel faces, readable 3-4-tone material shading, navy-violet shadows, approximately 4.5 to 5 heads tall for humans. Avoid smooth outlined anime illustrations, avoid tiny super-deformed chibis.
Deliver ONE square transparent RGBA atlas, EXACTLY 16 separated full-body sprites in a strict 4 columns x 4 rows grid in reading order. Each sprite centered in its own cell with generous completely transparent gutters (at least 15% of cell width), head, feet, hands and props entirely contained within the cell. All face right or right three-quarter toward the opponent. No background, no fake checkerboard, no floor/shadow, no frame labels or text, no painted skill effects. Consistent character model, head size and limb lengths in all frames. First three idle poses keep the SAME planted feet and hip position: subtle torso breathing and one blink only, NO horizontal sway or relocation.
Frame list in row-major order:
0 alert idle; 1 inhale idle, same feet; 2 blink idle, same feet;
3 normal attack wind-up; 4 advancing normal attack; 5 normal attack release; 6 extended contact pose;
7 follow-through; 8 recovery; 9 special preparation; 10 special release; 11 special recovery;
12 defensive guard; 13 small hit reaction; 14 defeated kneeling/slumped (non-gory); 15 unique final pose specified below.
Each pose must read distinctly and fit in its own cell. Retain visible pixel construction at normal display size. No other characters.
Yuji Itadori: pink short spiky hair, no Sukuna tattoos, dark navy high-collar school uniform with RED hood and cuffs, red-black high-top shoes, athletic teenage build. No weapons. Normal attack frames 3-8: compact boxing stance, hip-driven straight punch, front foot planted at contact, recover to boxing guard. Special frames 9-11: powerful low stance, shoulder drawn back, committed hook punch for Black Flash (render only the body, the engine adds black/red electricity). Frame 15 cheerful upright victory with clenched fist. Clearly two arms/hands in every upright stance.

